So my roughly two-billionth attempt to win with a Monk was going
rather well. Exp. level 15, 118 HP, AC -13, and I had not yet broken
vegetarian or weaponless content. A +5 helm o'brilliance and ring
o'slow digestion lead to a prolonged summon-and-sacrifice frenzy on a
level 6 altar. Got lots of weapons which I stashed for possible later
use (Vorpal Blade, Mjollnir, Fire and Frost Brand were the notables),
and several spellbooks.

I had built up a huge potential polypile but had not yet found a wand
of polymorph, nor Ludios. Lich on Level 22 scared me from going
further in the dungeon before improving my armor (I had not yet done
the quest either, fearing Master Kaen's toughness). Eventually a naga
disintegrated my gloves, and wouldn't you know there were none in the
polypile. Scared that I'd hit a cockatrice barehanded by mistake, I
decided to head back to the minetown, remembering that there might be
some gloves there. Got up to level 2 where the dungeon branch was, ran
into a floating eye. No reflection. DYWYPI...

Several dead monks later, stepped on a polytrap and became a
nalfeshnee. Annoyed that my robe was destroyed but figured I'd enjoy
being a demon for a change. No #monster abilities, but still got the
message, "Some hell-p has arrived!" and lo and behold I had my own pet
nalfeshnee. Invisible Ralph the Nalfeshnee was a super companion,
always available at the blow of my magic whistle to beat up anything
in my path, and self-healing thanks to his spellcasting abilities.
Chatted with him once for fun and he muttered a cantrip. :-)

Back at the minetown, went to the co-aligned altar and he and the
priestess started duking it out. I thought maybe I should keep her
alive for awhile longer since it was a sanctuary and I could also
later bribe her to get a lower AC, but I was too much enjoying
watching them hit and then retreat to cast healing spells on
themselves. While I was enjoying the show a cockatrice wandered by.
Frightened that my super-pet would soon become a demon-statue, I gave
the 'trice a karate chop. Oops, I hadn't noticed that when I lost that
robe from the polytrap, I lost my gloves too. DYWYPI...

Worse, the first YASD above left no bones (being on level 2), and my
second *did*, meaning the now not-so-friendly Ralph may be there to
greet me, ere I return to the Minetown. (Though assuming I can tame or
get past him somehow, there's a magic lamp waiting entombed in my
statue in the sanctuary...)

